# LungLens Cursor Rules

## Read Before Editing

- Development is already in progress. Do not rewrite working files from scratch.
- Before coding:
  1) scan current code structure and behavior,
  2) compare against architecture intent,
  3) report aligned/misaligned/missing items,
  4) make gentle, minimal adjustments.

## System Boundaries

- Frontend (Next.js on Vercel) and backend (FastAPI on HF Spaces) are separate systems.
- Frontend never runs ML inference and never loads model weights.
- Backend owns preprocessing, inference, gate logic, and report synthesis APIs.
- Models are trained in Colab and exported to backend runtime; no training scripts required in app runtime.

## API and Contract Guardrails

- Keep backend responses JSON-only.
- Preserve working frontend contract unless a critical mismatch is explicitly approved.
- Keep error shape consistent: `{"success": false, "error": "<message>"}`.
- Maintain gate behavior:
  - show/require clinical questionnaire only when gate indicates continuation.
- Maintain required enums and stable key names consumed by frontend.

## Backend Responsibilities

- Accept raw uploaded image files from frontend.
- Perform backend-side validation (auth, type, size) and preprocessing.
- Keep CORS restricted to intended frontend domains via env vars.
- Keep secrets in environment/secrets, never hardcoded.
- Treat ML as core product behavior, not optional scaffolding:
  - prioritize root-cause fixes for model loading/inference issues,
  - do not silently bypass real models with mock-only workarounds unless explicitly approved as temporary,
  - document any temporary fallback and create a clear path back to real model execution.

## Warm-Up and Health

- Ensure a lightweight health endpoint is available for frontend warm-up ping.
- Warm-up call is non-blocking from frontend perspective.

## LLM and Safety Constraints

- LLM output must synthesize model outputs; avoid definitive diagnosis wording.
- Always include disclaimer language in user-facing report sections.

## Change Management

- Keep existing custom UI/UX and styling decisions unless conflicting with core rules.
- If uncertain whether behavior is intentional, ask before changing.
- Prefer additive aliases/adapters over breaking endpoint or schema changes.
